NumPy fallback for slab sampling when the volume-cartographer bindings are missing.

Why: volume_slab_extractor.py imports `vc` for Volume.sample_planes / sample_coords.
Those bindings need vc_core and do not build on macOS yet (open PR #1975). The other
`vc` piece the dataset needs, vc.grid_raycast, is a self-contained source file and
builds alone with nanobind (windeval/native/CMakeLists.txt).

What: if `from vc import Volume` fails, use numpy_volume.py, which reads the zarr
array with zarr-python and follows ChunkedPlaneSampler's requested-level sampling
(XYZ coordinates, sentinel handling, fill value outside the array, float32 trilinear
blend clamped and truncated to uint8). Known difference: zarr returns the fill value
for absent chunks, where the C++ sampler zeroes any sample with a corner in an
absent chunk.

Checked: slab images bit-identical to windeval's chunk-level sampler on 8 PHerc0139
slabs (50.3 M voxels); that sampler matches scipy's trilinear interpolation within
one grey level. Not checked against the C++ sampler itself (no macOS build).

